<date>2026-11-07</date>
<releaseinfo>0.1.0</releaseinfo>

<abstract>
<para>
&kappname; is a small application for the Trinity Desktop Environment that
lets you search, browse and watch YouTube videos without a web browser.
</para>
</abstract>

<keywordset>
<keyword>TDE</keyword>
<keyword>Trinity</keyword>
<keyword>YouTube</keyword>
<keyword>video</keyword>
<keyword>mpv</keyword>
<keyword>yt-dlp</keyword>
<keyword>tde-youtube</keyword>
</keywordset>

</bookinfo>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<chapter id="introduction">
<title>Introduction</title>

<para>
&kappname; is a native &tde; application for browsing and playing YouTube
videos. You type a search into the tool bar, pick a video from the list of
results with their thumbnails, and it plays right inside the window. You can
keep videos you like in your <emphasis>Favourites</emphasis> and find videos
you have watched before in your <emphasis>History</emphasis>.
</para>

<para>
&kappname; does not talk to YouTube itself. It relies on two well known
free programs:
</para>

<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>
&ytdlp; searches YouTube and reads information about videos, channels and
playlists. No YouTube account or <acronym>API</acronym> key is needed.
</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>
&mpv; plays the videos. &kappname; embeds the &mpv; video window and
controls it remotely, so play/pause, seeking and volume work from the
&kappname; window.
</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>

<sect1 id="features">
<title>Features</title>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>Search YouTube, with a remembered search history.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Open the address of a video, playlist or channel directly.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Result lists with thumbnails, duration, channel and view count.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Video player embedded in the main window, or in a separate &mpv; window.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Play/pause, stop, seek, volume and full screen mode.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Choice of video quality, from 360p up to the best available, or audio only.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Video details with the full description, likes and upload date.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Favourites and watch history, stored locally.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Show all videos of a channel with one click.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Copy a video's address, or open it in your web browser.</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>Configurable keyboard shortcuts and tool bars, like every &tde; application.</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="disclaimer">
<title>Please Note</title>
<para>
&kappname; was largely written with the help of an AI coding assistant
(it is <quote>vibe coded</quote>). The code has not been audited. It is
provided as is, without any warranty; use it at your own risk.
</para>
<para>
&kappname; is not affiliated with, endorsed or sponsored by YouTube or
Google. <quote>YouTube</quote> is a trademark of Google LLC. Please respect
YouTube's terms of service and the rights of the people who make the videos.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="requirements">
<title>Requirements</title>
<para>
Besides the &tde; libraries, &kappname; needs:
</para>
<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para>
<command>yt-dlp</command> &mdash; <ulink url="https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp">https://github.com/yt-dlp/yt-dlp</ulink>.
YouTube changes often, so keep &ytdlp; up to date. Distribution packages
can lag behind; if searching or playing stops working, install the latest
release.
</para></listitem>
<listitem><para>
<command>mpv</command> &mdash; <ulink url="https://mpv.io">https://mpv.io</ulink>, version 0.35 or newer is recommended.
</para></listitem>
</itemizedlist>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<chapter id="using">
<title>Using &kappname;</title>

<sect1 id="main-window">
<title>The Main Window</title>

<screenshot>
<screeninfo>The &kappname; main window</screeninfo>
<mediaobject>
<imageobject><imagedata fileref="main-window.png" format="PNG"/></imageobject>
<textobject><phrase>The &kappname; main window</phrase></textobject>
</mediaobject>
</screenshot>

<para>The main window is made of these parts:</para>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term>The search box</term>
<listitem><para>
In the tool bar. Type what you are looking for and press &Enter;. Earlier
searches can be picked from its drop down list.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term>The video lists</term>
<listitem><para>
On the left, with three tabs: <guilabel>Search</guilabel> (the results of the
last search), <guilabel>Favourites</guilabel> and <guilabel>History</guilabel>.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term>The player</term>
<listitem><para>
At the top right, with the player controls below the picture.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term>The details pane</term>
<listitem><para>
At the bottom right. It shows the title, channel, duration, views, likes,
upload date and the description of the selected video. Links in the
description open in your web browser.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
<para>
The borders between the parts can be dragged to make them larger or
smaller; &kappname; remembers the layout.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="searching">
<title>Searching</title>
<para>
Click into the search box (or press <keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>),
type a few words and press &Enter;. The results appear in the
<guilabel>Search</guilabel> tab as soon as they arrive, and their thumbnails
are loaded in the background. The first result is selected automatically,
and its details are shown on the right.
</para>
<para>
By default 20 videos are listed. Click <guibutton>More Results</guibutton>
below the list (or press <keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>M</keycap></keycombo>)
to load more. The number of results per search can be changed in the
<link linkend="config-playback">settings</link>.
</para>

<sect2 id="opening-urls">
<title>Opening Addresses</title>
<para>
Instead of search words you can paste the address of a YouTube video,
playlist or channel into the search box, or use
<menuchoice><guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open URL...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>.
The address of a single video (for example
<literal>https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=...</literal> or
<literal>https://youtu.be/...</literal>) starts playing right away. A
playlist or channel address lists its videos; for a channel these are its
most recent uploads.
</para>
<para>
You can also start &kappname; with an address on the command line, see
<xref linkend="commandline"/>.
</para>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="channels">
<title>Videos of a Channel</title>
<para>
To see more videos from the same channel, select a video and choose
<menuchoice><guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Channel Videos</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
(<keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>U</keycap></keycombo>), or use the
context menu of the video.
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="watching">
<title>Watching Videos</title>

<screenshot>
<screeninfo>Watching a video</screeninfo>
<mediaobject>
<imageobject><imagedata fileref="playing.png" format="PNG"/></imageobject>
<textobject><phrase>Watching a video</phrase></textobject>
</mediaobject>
</screenshot>

<para>
Double-click a video, or select it and press &Enter;, to play it. It takes a
moment until &ytdlp; has found the video stream; the player shows
<guilabel>Loading</guilabel> meanwhile. Every video you play is added to
your <link linkend="favourites-history">History</link>.
</para>

<para>The controls below the picture are, from left to right:</para>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guiicon>Play/Pause</guiicon></term>
<listitem><para>Pauses or resumes the video (<keycap>Space</keycap>).</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guiicon>Stop</guiicon></term>
<listitem><para>Stops playback (<keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>.</keycap></keycombo>).</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term>Position slider</term>
<listitem><para>
Shows how far the video has played. Drag it, or click into it, to jump to
another position. <keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Right</keysym></keycombo>
and <keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Left</keysym></keycombo> skip ten seconds forward
and backward.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term>Time</term>
<listitem><para>The current position and the length of the video, or <guilabel>Buffering...</guilabel>.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term>Volume slider</term>
<listitem><para>
Sets the volume (also <keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Up</keysym></keycombo> and
<keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Down</keysym></keycombo>). The volume is remembered.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guiicon>Full Screen</guiicon></term>
<listitem><para>Switches full screen mode on and off.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>

<sect2 id="fullscreen">
<title>Full Screen Mode</title>
<para>
In full screen mode only the video and the player controls are shown. Enter
it with the <guiicon>Full Screen</guiicon> button,
<keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo>, by
double-clicking the video or by pressing <keycap>F</keycap> while the video
has the keyboard focus. Leave it the same way or with &Esc;.
</para>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="external-player">
<title>Playing in a Separate Window</title>
<para>
<menuchoice><guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Play in External Player</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
(<keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo>) plays the
selected video in its own &mpv; window. All &mpv; keyboard shortcuts work
there. The &kappname; player controls still control it. If you always want
a separate window, switch off <guilabel>Embed the video in the main window</guilabel>
in the <link linkend="config-playback">settings</link>.
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="favourites-history">
<title>Favourites and History</title>

<screenshot>
<screeninfo>Favourites</screeninfo>
<mediaobject>
<imageobject><imagedata fileref="favourites.png" format="PNG"/></imageobject>
<textobject><phrase>The Favourites tab</phrase></textobject>
</mediaobject>
</screenshot>

<para>
To keep a video, select it and choose
<menuchoice><guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add to Favourites</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
(<keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>D</keycap></keycombo>), click the star
in the tool bar, or use the context menu. The same command removes a
favourite again. Your favourites are listed in the
<guilabel>Favourites</guilabel> tab, newest first.
</para>
<para>
The <guilabel>History</guilabel> tab lists the videos you have played,
most recent first. The history can be switched off, limited, or cleared
on the <link linkend="config-history">History</link> page of the settings.
</para>
<para>
In both tabs, <menuchoice><guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Remove from List</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
(<keycap>Del</keycap>) removes the selected video from that list.
</para>
<para>
Favourites and history are kept on your computer only, in the file
<filename>~/.trinity/share/config/tde-youtube-libraryrc</filename>.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="context-menu">
<title>The Context Menu</title>
<para>
Click a video with the &RMB; for a menu with the most important commands:
<guimenuitem>Play</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Play in External Player</guimenuitem>,
<guimenuitem>Add to Favourites</guimenuitem>, <guimenuitem>Show Channel Videos</guimenuitem>,
<guimenuitem>Copy Video Address</guimenuitem> and <guimenuitem>Open in Web Browser</guimenuitem>.
</para>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<chapter id="configuration">
<title>Configuring &kappname;</title>
<para>
Choose <menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure TDE YouTube...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>
to open the settings dialog. Like in every &tde; application you can also
change the keyboard shortcuts
(<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Shortcuts...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>)
and the tool bar
(<menuchoice><guimenu>Settings</guimenu><guimenuitem>Configure Toolbars...</guimenuitem></menuchoice>).
</para>

<sect1 id="config-playback">
<title>Playback</title>
<screenshot>
<screeninfo>The Playback page</screeninfo>
<mediaobject>
<imageobject><imagedata fileref="settings-playback.png" format="PNG"/></imageobject>
<textobject><phrase>The Playback page of the settings dialog</phrase></textobject>
</mediaobject>
</screenshot>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Preferred quality</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
The highest video resolution to request: <guilabel>Best available</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Up to 1080p</guilabel> (the default), <guilabel>Up to 720p</guilabel>,
<guilabel>Up to 480p</guilabel>, <guilabel>Up to 360p</guilabel> or
<guilabel>Audio only</guilabel>. Lower resolutions need less bandwidth and
processing power.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Embed the video in the main window</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
When checked (the default), videos play inside the &kappname; window.
Otherwise &mpv; opens its own window.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Extra mpv options</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
Additional command line options for &mpv;, separated by spaces, for example
<userinput>--hwdec=auto</userinput> to use hardware video decoding. See
<citerefentry><refentrytitle>mpv</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Results per search</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
How many videos a search lists, and how many more <guibutton>More Results</guibutton> adds (5 to 100).
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="config-programs">
<title>Programs</title>
<screenshot>
<screeninfo>The Programs page</screeninfo>
<mediaobject>
<imageobject><imagedata fileref="settings-programs.png" format="PNG"/></imageobject>
<textobject><phrase>The Programs page of the settings dialog</phrase></textobject>
</mediaobject>
</screenshot>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>yt-dlp</guilabel> and <guilabel>mpv</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
The commands used to run &ytdlp; and &mpv;. A plain command name is looked
up in your <envar>PATH</envar>; you can also enter a full path, for example
to use a newer &ytdlp; installed in your home folder.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Use cookies from browser</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
Sometimes YouTube refuses to answer unless you are signed in, and
&kappname; reports <quote>Sign in to confirm you're not a bot</quote>.
Choose a web browser in which you are signed in to YouTube, and &ytdlp;
will use its cookies. You can also type
<userinput>browser:profile</userinput>, for example
<userinput>firefox:default-release</userinput>.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Cookies file</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>
Alternatively, a file with cookies in the Netscape
<filename>cookies.txt</filename> format.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="config-history">
<title>History</title>
<screenshot>
<screeninfo>The History page</screeninfo>
<mediaobject>
<imageobject><imagedata fileref="settings-history.png" format="PNG"/></imageobject>
<textobject><phrase>The History page of the settings dialog</phrase></textobject>
</mediaobject>
</screenshot>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Remember watched videos</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Whether played videos are added to the history.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guilabel>Maximum history entries</guilabel></term>
<listitem><para>Older entries are removed when the history grows beyond this size.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guibutton>Clear History</guibutton></term>
<listitem><para>Removes all videos from the history.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><guibutton>Clear Thumbnail Cache</guibutton></term>
<listitem><para>
Deletes the downloaded thumbnails, which are kept in
<filename>~/.trinity/share/cache/tde-youtube/thumbs</filename>.
</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<chapter id="commands">
<title>Command Reference</title>

<sect1 id="menus">
<title>Menus</title>

<sect2 id="menu-file">
<title>The <guimenu>File</guimenu> Menu</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>O</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open URL...</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Opens the address of a YouTube video, playlist or channel. An address on the clipboard is suggested.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>Q</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>File</guimenu><guimenuitem>Quit</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Quits &kappname;.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="menu-search">
<title>The <guimenu>Search</guimenu> Menu</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Search</guimenu><guimenuitem>Focus Search Box</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Moves the keyboard focus to the search box.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycap>F6</keycap></shortcut>
<guimenu>Search</guimenu><guimenuitem>Search</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Searches for the text in the search box.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>M</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Search</guimenu><guimenuitem>More Results</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Adds more results to the search list.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="menu-video">
<title>The <guimenu>Video</guimenu> Menu</title>
<para>These commands work on the selected video, or on the playing one if no video is selected.</para>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Play</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Plays the video in the main window.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>P</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Play in External Player</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Plays the video in a separate &mpv; window.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>D</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Add to Favourites</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Adds the video to your favourites, or removes it if it already is one.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycap>Del</keycap></shortcut>
<guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Remove from List</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Removes the video from the favourites or the history, depending on the tab shown.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>U</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Show Channel Videos</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Lists the latest videos of the video's channel.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>C</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Copy Video Address</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Copies the video's YouTube address to the clipboard.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>B</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Video</guimenu><guimenuitem>Open in Web Browser</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Opens the video's page in your web browser.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="menu-player">
<title>The <guimenu>Player</guimenu> Menu</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycap>Space</keycap></shortcut>
<guimenu>Player</guimenu><guimenuitem>Pause</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Pauses or resumes playback.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>.</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Player</guimenu><guimenuitem>Stop</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Stops playback.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Left</keysym></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Player</guimenu><guimenuitem>Skip Backward</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Jumps back ten seconds.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Right</keysym></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Player</guimenu><guimenuitem>Skip Forward</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Jumps forward ten seconds.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Up</keysym></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Player</guimenu><guimenuitem>Volume Up</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Makes the sound louder.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keysym>Down</keysym></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>Player</guimenu><guimenuitem>Volume Down</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Makes the sound quieter.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="menu-view">
<title>The <guimenu>View</guimenu> Menu</title>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>1</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Search Results</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Shows the <guilabel>Search</guilabel> tab.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>2</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Favourites</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Shows the <guilabel>Favourites</guilabel> tab.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;<keycap>3</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>History</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Shows the <guilabel>History</guilabel> tab.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><menuchoice><shortcut><keycombo action="simul">&Ctrl;&Shift;<keycap>F</keycap></keycombo></shortcut>
<guimenu>View</guimenu><guimenuitem>Full Screen Mode</guimenuitem></menuchoice></term>
<listitem><para>Switches full screen mode on and off.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
</sect2>

<sect2 id="menu-settings-help">
<title>The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> and <guimenu>Help</guimenu> Menus</title>
<para>
&kappname; has the common &tde; <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> and
<guimenu>Help</guimenu> menus. The <guimenu>Settings</guimenu> menu also has
<guimenuitem>Configure TDE YouTube...</guimenuitem>, described in
<xref linkend="configuration"/>. For the other entries, see the chapters on
the <ulink url="help:/khelpcenter/menus.html#menus-settings">Settings menu</ulink>
and <ulink url="help:/khelpcenter/menus.html#menus-help">Help menu</ulink> of
the &tde; fundamentals.
</para>
</sect2>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="commandline">
<title>Command Line Options</title>
<para>
<cmdsynopsis>
<command>tde-youtube</command>
<group choice="opt"><option>-s, --search</option> <replaceable>query</replaceable></group>
<arg choice="opt"><replaceable>URL</replaceable></arg>
<arg choice="opt" rep="repeat">generic TDE and TQt options</arg>
</cmdsynopsis>
</para>
<variablelist>
<varlistentry>
<term><option>-s</option>, <option>--search</option> <replaceable>query</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Searches YouTube for <replaceable>query</replaceable> on start-up.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
<varlistentry>
<term><replaceable>URL</replaceable></term>
<listitem><para>Opens a YouTube address: a video starts playing, a playlist or channel is listed.</para></listitem>
</varlistentry>
</variablelist>
<para>
<command>tde-youtube --help-all</command> lists all options. The manual page
<citerefentry><refentrytitle>tde-youtube</refentrytitle><manvolnum>1</manvolnum></citerefentry>
describes them in more detail.
</para>
</sect1>
</chapter>

<!-- ================================================================== -->
<chapter id="faq">
<title>Questions and Answers</title>

<qandaset id="faqlist">
<qandaentry>
<question><para>Nothing plays and I see <quote>Sign in to confirm you're not a bot</quote>.</para></question>
<answer><para>
YouTube sometimes refuses requests that are not from a signed in user,
especially from shared or data centre networks. Select a web browser in
which you are signed in to YouTube under
<guilabel>Use cookies from browser</guilabel> on the
<link linkend="config-programs">Programs</link> page of the settings.
</para></answer>
</qandaentry>

<qandaentry>
<question><para>Searching or playing suddenly stopped working.</para></question>
<answer><para>
YouTube changes frequently and old versions of &ytdlp; stop working. Update
&ytdlp; to the latest release, for example with
<userinput><command>yt-dlp</command> <option>-U</option></userinput> (if it was installed
from its release page) or <userinput><command>pipx</command> upgrade yt-dlp</userinput>.
You can point &kappname; at a newer copy on the
<link linkend="config-programs">Programs</link> page.
</para></answer>
</qandaentry>

<qandaentry>
<question><para>&kappname; says it could not run yt-dlp or mpv.</para></question>
<answer><para>
Install the program with your package manager, or enter its full path on the
<link linkend="config-programs">Programs</link> page of the settings.
</para></answer>
</qandaentry>

<qandaentry>
<question><para>Videos stutter or use a lot of CPU.</para></question>
<answer><para>
Choose a lower <guilabel>Preferred quality</guilabel>, or add
<userinput>--hwdec=auto</userinput> to the <guilabel>Extra mpv options</guilabel>
to let your graphics card decode the video.
</para></answer>
</qandaentry>

<qandaentry>
<question><para>Can I download videos with &kappname;?</para></question>
<answer><para>
No. &kappname; only streams videos. Please respect YouTube's terms of service
and the rights of the creators.
</para></answer>
</qandaentry>

<qandaentry>
<question><para>Where does &kappname; store its data?</para></question>
<answer><para>
Settings in <filename>~/.trinity/share/config/tde-youtuberc</filename>,
favourites and history in <filename>~/.trinity/share/config/tde-youtube-libraryrc</filename>,
and thumbnails in <filename>~/.trinity/share/cache/tde-youtube/thumbs</filename>.
Nothing is sent anywhere except the requests &ytdlp; and &mpv; make to YouTube.
</para></answer>
</qandaentry>
</qandaset>
</chapter>

