<!-- ================================================================== -->
<appendix id="installation">
<title>Installation</title>

<sect1 id="getting-tde-youtube">
<title>How to obtain &kappname;</title>
<para>
The source code and Debian packages built for each change are available at
<ulink url="https://github.com/Yjlion/tde-youtube">https://github.com/Yjlion/tde-youtube</ulink>.
Install a package with
<userinput><command>sudo apt install</command> ./tde-youtube_*.deb</userinput>,
which also installs &ytdlp; and &mpv;.
</para>
</sect1>

<sect1 id="compilation">
<title>Compilation and Installation</title>
<para>
You need the &tde; development files (<literal>tdelibs14-trinity-dev</literal>,
<literal>libtqt3-mt-dev</literal>, <literal>tqt3-dev-tools</literal> and
<literal>tde-cmake</literal> on Debian and Ubuntu), <application>CMake</application> and a C++ compiler.
</para>
<screen width="40">
<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>mkdir</command> build &amp;&amp; <command>cd</command> build</userinput>
<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>cmake</command> .. -DCMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX=/opt/trinity</userinput>
<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>make</command></userinput>
<prompt>%</prompt> <userinput><command>sudo make</command> install</userinput>
</screen>
</sect1>
</appendix>

&documentation.index;
</book>
